 oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Watchpoints: Stability Pool depth vs circulating debt, liquidation discount dynamics, LUSD liquidity/integration health, and oracle/price feed assumptions under fast ETH moves. (Liquity Docs)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Stablecoin credit primitive (ETH-backed) and liquidation-mechanics showcase (Stability Pool vs auctions) (Liquity)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active (Liquity V1 live; Liquity V2 under separate documentation track) (Liquity)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets criteria: onchain borrowing, collateralized credit issuance (LUSD), and protocol-enforced solvency + liquidation mechanics. (Liquity Docs)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "High (LUSD is a core collateral-backed stablecoin in Ethereum DeFi; Liquity is a major CDP primitive) (CryptoEQ)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "ETH liquidity, liquidator/arb participation, Stability Pool deposits, and market liquidity for LUSD integrations (Liquity Docs)"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();
